{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Make yourself a seraph.</b> And it is written: ״ויעש משה נחש נחשת״ — 'And Moses made a serpent of bronze.' Our master Moses, peace be upon him, understood that the will of the Holy One, blessed be He, was to make a נחש (serpent), but He did not wish to mention it by its proper name, which is נחש, because it was the cause of sin and brought death to the world. Therefore He said 'seraph' (שרף), mentioning it by an epithet, for it is the possessor of burning venom. And as for why He said 'for yourself' (לך) and did not say simply 'make a seraph' — the Holy One, blessed be He, said: concerning what they spoke against Him, 'I forgive them in the merit of your prayer'; but what they spoke against you — 'make yourself a seraph' — you must perform a deed with your own hands, so that it may be publicized how grave it is before Him who speaks against the prophets.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:31.576086913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}